      "draft": "Jessa Rook looked down at the boots held out toward her, then back up at Nicco. Her expression didn't change much — the same steady, measuring look she'd worn since the exchange began.\n\n\"I gave those to you,\" she said, her voice low and unhurried. \"They're yours. I've got my own.\"\n\nShe didn't reach for them. Her hands stayed where they were, one resting near the notebook tucked in her belt, the other loose at her side. A couple of passers-by moved along the edge of the square behind her, paying no attention.\n\n\"Keep them,\" she said. It wasn't a suggestion phrased as one.",
